# The following settings were initially written by the github account MOZGII. They 
# were modified by Maven Dev for a different repo structure and to add plugin settings.

# This .gitignore is designed for the root repo dir containing the Unreal Engine
# project dir and a "NonEngineContent" dir. The repo should look something like:
#	>.git (hidden dir)
#	>.github/
#	>NonEngineContent/
#	>UE_Project/
#	>.gitignore (this file)
#	>.gitattributes (if using git lfs)
#	>README.md

# Note that any files/dirs added aside from the ones mentioned above are likely
# excluded automatically by these settings, and editing would be required.

# Last editied 17/11/2026 by Maven Dev.

# Ignore all files by default, but keep all dirs.
*
!*/

# Do not ignore git files in the root of the repo.
!/.git*

# Do not ignore the read me file.
!README.md

# Do not ignore current project's `.uproject`.
!*/*.uproject

# Do not ignore the steam_appid if the project has one
!*/*steam_appid.txt

# Do not ignore source and config dirs.
!*/Source/**
!*/Config/**

# Plugin dirs are a project in of themselves, so they get extra specificity.
!*/Plugins/*/*.uplugin
!*/Plugins/*/Config/**
!*/Plugins/*/Source/**
!*/Plugins/*/Resources/**

# Only allow .uasset and .umap files from the Content dir.
# They're tracked by git-lfs, don't forget to track other
# files if adding them here.
!*/Content/**/*.uasset
!*/Content/**/*.umap

# Allow any files from the NonEngineContent dir.
# Any file in the NonEngineContent dir will be managed by git lfs.
# This is where art assets (like .fbx) would be stored.
!/NonEngineContent/**/*
